/*!
\page page_stSvtHitCollection StSvtHitCollection

\ref StSvtHitCollection is the top-level container for all reconstructed hits in the STAR Silicon
Vertex Tracker (SVT). Hits are stored in a four-level hierarchy —
<b>barrel → ladder → wafer → hit</b> — mirroring the physical geometry of the SVT's three
concentric silicon barrels. The three supporting classes, \ref StSvtBarrelHitCollection,
\ref StSvtLadderHitCollection, and \ref StSvtWaferHitCollection, are internal nodes of that
hierarchy and are not used independently.

\section sec_svt_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\verbatim
StSvtHitCollection            (top level, 3 barrels)
└── StSvtBarrelHitCollection      (one per barrel; 8, 12, or 16 ladders)
    └── StSvtLadderHitCollection      (one per ladder; 4, 6, or 7 wafers)
        └── StSvtWaferHitCollection       (one per wafer, holds StSvtHit* pointers)
\endverbatim

All four classes inherit from StObject.

\section sec_svt_containment Containment Model

- \ref StSvtHitCollection holds an embedded array of 3 \ref StSvtBarrelHitCollection objects
  (<tt>mBarrels[3]</tt>).
- Each \ref StSvtBarrelHitCollection holds an embedded array of up to 16
  \ref StSvtLadderHitCollection objects (<tt>mLadders[16]</tt>); the active count is
  barrel-dependent (8, 12, or 16).
- Each \ref StSvtLadderHitCollection holds an embedded array of up to 7
  \ref StSvtWaferHitCollection objects (<tt>mWafers[7]</tt>); the active count is
  barrel-dependent (4, 6, or 7).
- Each \ref StSvtWaferHitCollection holds a dynamic <tt>StSPtrVecSvtHit mHits</tt> vector of
  pointers to \ref StSvtHit objects.

\subsection subsec_svt_geometry Barrel-Dependent Geometry

| Barrel index | Ladders per barrel | Wafers per ladder |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | 8 | 4 |
| 1 | 12 | 6 |
| 2 | 16 | 7 |

This configuration is established in the \ref StSvtHitCollection constructor, which calls
<tt>setBarrelNumber(i)</tt> on each barrel and ladder collection. The barrel number drives the
<tt>numberOfLadders()</tt> and <tt>numberOfWafers()</tt> switch statements in those classes.

\ref StSvtHitCollection::addHit "addHit(StSvtHit*)" routes an \ref StSvtHit into the correct
<tt>mHits</tt> vector using the hit's own 1-based <tt>barrel()</tt>, <tt>ladder()</tt>, and
<tt>wafer()</tt> accessors, converting internally to 0-based array indices. The public accessor
methods <tt>barrel()</tt>, <tt>ladder()</tt>, and <tt>wafer()</tt> all use <b>0-based</b> indices.

\section sec_svt_ownership Object Ownership

\subsection subsec_svt_subcoll Sub-collection Storage
\ref StSvtBarrelHitCollection, \ref StSvtLadderHitCollection, and \ref StSvtWaferHitCollection
objects are <b>stack-allocated as plain arrays</b> inside their parent. They are not heap-allocated
and must not be deleted by the caller. The arrays are sized to the maximum capacity
(<tt>mMaxNumberOfLadders = 16</tt>, <tt>mMaxNumberOfWafers = 7</tt>); only entries with indices
below the barrel-specific active count are meaningful.

\subsection subsec_svt_hits Hit Storage — StSPtrVecSvtHit
The per-wafer hit vector is of type <tt>StSPtrVecSvtHit</tt>, a <em>smart-pointer vector</em>.
\ref StSvtWaferHitCollection::~StSvtWaferHitCollection "~StSvtWaferHitCollection()" iterates over
the vector and explicitly <tt>delete</tt>s each <tt>StSvtHit*</tt>. This explicit deletion is
required because \ref StSvtHit uses a custom <tt>new</tt>/<tt>delete</tt> via
<tt>StMemoryPool</tt>.

\warning Do <b>not</b> <tt>delete</tt> \ref StSvtHit pointers obtained from the collection.
Ownership belongs to \ref StSvtWaferHitCollection; external deletion will cause a double-free.

\subsection subsec_svt_framework Framework Ownership
\ref StSvtHitCollection itself is owned by the StEvent framework (via the
<tt>St_DataSet</tt>/<tt>StXRefMain</tt> mechanism). When registered with StEvent via
<tt>StEvent::setSvtHitCollection()</tt>, ownership transfers to the framework, which handles
cleanup. <tt>StSvtHitCollection::~StSvtHitCollection()</tt>,
<tt>StSvtBarrelHitCollection::~StSvtBarrelHitCollection()</tt>, and
<tt>StSvtLadderHitCollection::~StSvtLadderHitCollection()</tt> are all no-ops; only
\ref StSvtWaferHitCollection performs explicit hit cleanup.

\section sec_svt_members Data Members

\subsection subsec_svt_members_top StSvtHitCollection
- <tt>enum { mNumberOfBarrels = 3 }</tt> — Fixed number of SVT barrels.
- <tt>StSvtBarrelHitCollection mBarrels[3]</tt> — Embedded array of per-barrel collections.

\subsection subsec_svt_members_barrel StSvtBarrelHitCollection
- <tt>enum { mMaxNumberOfLadders = 16 }</tt> — Array capacity; active count is 8, 12, or 16.
- <tt>Int_t mBarrelNumber</tt> — 0-based barrel index; drives <tt>numberOfLadders()</tt>.
- <tt>StSvtLadderHitCollection mLadders[16]</tt> — Embedded array of ladder collections.

\subsection subsec_svt_members_ladder StSvtLadderHitCollection
- <tt>enum { mMaxNumberOfWafers = 7 }</tt> — Array capacity; active count is 4, 6, or 7.
- <tt>Int_t mBarrelNumber</tt> — 0-based barrel index; drives <tt>numberOfWafers()</tt>.
- <tt>StSvtWaferHitCollection mWafers[7]</tt> — Embedded array of wafer collections.

\subsection subsec_svt_members_wafer StSvtWaferHitCollection
- <tt>StSPtrVecSvtHit mHits</tt> — Dynamic vector of pointers to \ref StSvtHit objects on this
  wafer.

\section sec_svt_methods Key Methods

\subsection subsec_svt_methods_top StSvtHitCollection
- <tt>bool addHit(StSvtHit*)</tt> — Routes a hit into the correct barrel/ladder/wafer
  sub-collection. Returns <tt>false</tt> if null or indices out of range.
- <tt>unsigned int numberOfHits() const</tt> — Total hits across all barrels, ladders, and wafers.
- <tt>unsigned int numberOfBarrels() const</tt> — Returns 3.
- <tt>StSvtBarrelHitCollection* barrel(unsigned int)</tt> — Sub-collection at 0-based index, or
  <tt>nullptr</tt> if out of range.

\subsection subsec_svt_methods_barrel StSvtBarrelHitCollection
- <tt>unsigned int numberOfHits() const</tt> — Total hits in this barrel.
- <tt>unsigned int numberOfLadders() const</tt> — Active ladder count (8, 12, or 16).
- <tt>StSvtLadderHitCollection* ladder(unsigned int)</tt> — Sub-collection at 0-based index.
- <tt>void setBarrelNumber(int)</tt> — Sets barrel index; no-op if already set.

\subsection subsec_svt_methods_ladder StSvtLadderHitCollection
- <tt>unsigned int numberOfHits() const</tt> — Total hits on this ladder.
- <tt>unsigned int numberOfWafers() const</tt> — Active wafer count (4, 6, or 7).
- <tt>StSvtWaferHitCollection* wafer(unsigned int)</tt> — Sub-collection at 0-based index.
- <tt>void setBarrelNumber(int)</tt> — Sets parent barrel index; no-op if already set.

\subsection subsec_svt_methods_wafer StSvtWaferHitCollection
- <tt>StSPtrVecSvtHit& hits()</tt> — Mutable reference to the hit vector.
- <tt>const StSPtrVecSvtHit& hits() const</tt> — Const reference to the hit vector.

\section sec_svt_usage Usage Examples

\subsection subsec_svt_usage_iter Iterate Over All Hits

\code{.cpp}
StSvtHitCollection* svtColl = event->svtHitCollection();
if (!svtColl) return;

for (unsigned int iBarrel = 0; iBarrel < svtColl->numberOfBarrels(); ++iBarrel) {
    const StSvtBarrelHitCollection* barrel = svtColl->barrel(iBarrel);
    if (!barrel) continue;

    for (unsigned int iLadder = 0; iLadder < barrel->numberOfLadders(); ++iLadder) {
        const StSvtLadderHitCollection* ladder = barrel->ladder(iLadder);
        if (!ladder) continue;

        for (unsigned int iWafer = 0; iWafer < ladder->numberOfWafers(); ++iWafer) {
            const StSvtWaferHitCollection* wafer = ladder->wafer(iWafer);
            if (!wafer) continue;

            const StSPtrVecSvtHit& hits = wafer->hits();
            for (const StSvtHit* hit : hits) {
                // process hit -- do NOT delete hit
            }
        }
    }
}
\endcode

\subsection subsec_svt_usage_add Add a Hit (e.g. from a Maker)

\code{.cpp}
StSvtHit* hit = new StSvtHit(/*...*/);  // allocated via StSvtHit::operator new
svtColl->addHit(hit);                   // ownership transferred to the collection
// Do not delete 'hit' after this call.
\endcode

*/
